1
00:02:30,058 --> 00:02:35,058
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,058 --> 00:02:40,058
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,058 --> 00:02:44,058
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,058 --> 00:02:49,058
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,058 --> 00:02:52,058
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,058 --> 00:02:55,058
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,058 --> 00:02:58,058
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,058 --> 00:03:01,058
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:01,058 --> 00:03:04,058
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:07,058
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,058 --> 00:03:11,058
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,058 --> 00:03:15,058
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:18,058 --> 00:03:23,058
After losing his brother Ace during the War of the Best, Luffy was distraught.

14
00:03:23,058 --> 00:03:27,058
Me! King of the Pirates!

15
00:03:27,058 --> 00:03:33,058
He was soon surprised by Dark King Rayleigh's unexpected appearance at the Maiden Island.

16
00:03:33,058 --> 00:03:36,058
I may have another suggestion for you.

17
00:03:36,058 --> 00:03:38,058
After they learned of Ace's death at Marineford,

18
00:03:38,058 --> 00:03:43,058
the rest of the Straw Hats made haste to reunite with Luffy and offer their support.

19
00:03:47,058 --> 00:03:52,058
Encounter! The Great Swordsman Mihawk! Zoro's self-will deadly struggle!

20
00:03:52,058 --> 00:03:54,058
The Great SwordsmanOlive

21
00:03:54,058 --> 00:04:22,478
This is Gloom Island on the Grand Line.

22
00:04:22,478 --> 00:04:25,978
Home to the ruins of the Monkey Kingdom.

23
00:04:25,978 --> 00:04:29,258
An old castle remains from the long-dead empire.

24
00:04:29,258 --> 00:04:33,478
Despite its age, a well-known figure has made the castle his home.

25
00:04:33,478 --> 00:04:38,478
Why did Mario have to get himself killed?

26
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:49,138
You're being a pest.

27
00:04:49,138 --> 00:04:50,478
Go and cry somewhere else.

28
00:04:50,478 --> 00:04:52,478
How can you be so heartless when I'm grieving?

29
00:04:52,478 --> 00:04:55,478
Show some compassion, you big meanie!

30
00:04:55,478 --> 00:04:57,478
Do you have anything kind to say?

31
00:04:57,478 --> 00:04:58,478
Offer me a tissue!

32
00:04:58,478 --> 00:04:59,478
I'm your guest!

33
00:04:59,478 --> 00:05:01,478
Your manners are appalling!

34
00:05:01,478 --> 00:05:03,478
I never invited you.

35
00:05:03,478 --> 00:05:07,478
The two of you showed up and started living here without asking.

36
00:05:07,478 --> 00:05:11,478
Furthermore, this article is not credible.

37
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:12,478
What?

38
00:05:12,478 --> 00:05:15,478
But does that mean Moriya could still be alive?

39
00:05:15,478 --> 00:05:16,478
He made it out?

40
00:05:16,478 --> 00:05:19,478
A good question, now you ask.

41
00:05:19,478 --> 00:05:22,478
If he died, then I didn't see it.

42
00:05:22,478 --> 00:05:27,478
Although, if he did escape, then I didn't see that either, I'm afraid.

43
00:05:27,478 --> 00:05:31,478
But you think he might have survived and they're lying about it for some reason?

44
00:05:31,478 --> 00:05:32,478
Perhaps.

45
00:05:32,478 --> 00:05:33,478
Huh?

46
00:05:33,478 --> 00:05:38,478
What are you doing out of bed?

47
00:05:38,478 --> 00:05:39,478
You're hurt!

48
00:05:39,478 --> 00:05:40,478
Bad!

49
00:05:40,478 --> 00:05:41,478
Are you crazy?!

50
00:05:41,478 --> 00:05:44,478
Put those swords down, you moron!

51
00:05:46,478 --> 00:05:49,478
Don't tell me you're gonna try and fight them again!

52
00:05:49,478 --> 00:05:50,478
Give up!

53
00:05:50,478 --> 00:05:52,478
You're lucky you survived the first fight!

54
00:05:52,478 --> 00:05:53,478
Those baboons will murder you!

55
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,478
Shut up!

56
00:05:55,478 --> 00:05:57,478
Keep your nose out of my business!

57
00:05:57,478 --> 00:05:58,478
Got it?!

58
00:05:58,478 --> 00:05:59,478
How could you say such a cruel thing to me?!

59
00:05:59,478 --> 00:06:01,478
I dragged your stupid body all the way back here!

60
00:06:01,478 --> 00:06:03,478
Without my help, you'd beat Monkey Chow!

61
00:06:04,478 --> 00:06:05,478
Hawkeye...

62
00:06:10,478 --> 00:06:11,478
Give it a rest already!

63
00:06:11,478 --> 00:06:13,478
You can barely even walk!

64
00:06:13,478 --> 00:06:14,478
You're wounded.

65
00:06:14,478 --> 00:06:15,478
Stay here.

66
00:06:15,478 --> 00:06:17,478
Why are you in such a hurry?

67
00:06:17,478 --> 00:06:20,478
Have you forgotten?

68
00:06:20,478 --> 00:06:23,478
You told me what happened to my captain!

69
00:06:23,478 --> 00:06:24,478
I have to go!

70
00:06:25,478 --> 00:06:30,478
He should still be alive, but unfortunately he appears to be severely traumatized.

71
00:06:31,478 --> 00:06:33,478
Firefist Ace died.

72
00:06:34,478 --> 00:06:36,478
Right before Straw Hat's eyes.

73
00:06:37,478 --> 00:06:38,478
All this time...

74
00:06:39,478 --> 00:06:41,478
And I never even knew the war was happening.

75
00:06:42,478 --> 00:06:43,478
But Luffy's alright!

76
00:06:44,478 --> 00:06:45,478
Are you sure?

77
00:06:45,478 --> 00:06:46,478
Where is he now?!

78
00:06:47,478 --> 00:06:49,478
Can't you tell me anything else?!

79
00:06:50,478 --> 00:06:51,478
No, alas.

80
00:06:51,478 --> 00:06:52,478
That's all I know.

81
00:06:55,478 --> 00:06:56,478
Fine.

82
00:06:56,478 --> 00:06:57,478
Then I'll leave you alone.

83
00:07:00,478 --> 00:07:01,478
Hey, stupid!

84
00:07:01,478 --> 00:07:02,478
Hold on!

85
00:07:02,478 --> 00:07:05,478
You're never gonna make it to the shore without those baboon things attacking you!

86
00:07:05,478 --> 00:07:08,478
And even if you do get there, how are you gonna cross the sea?!

87
00:07:10,478 --> 00:07:14,478
If you want a boat, circle around the castle, west side.

88
00:07:17,478 --> 00:07:18,478
Thank you for that.

89
00:07:22,478 --> 00:07:23,478
Are you kidding me?!

90
00:07:23,478 --> 00:07:24,478
Dummy!

91
00:07:24,478 --> 00:07:27,478
That's the last time I saved you a grateful butt!

92
00:07:28,478 --> 00:07:30,478
You can bury your own corpse when they kill you!

93
00:07:30,478 --> 00:07:44,478
Luffy, although you just lost your brother, no matter what, I know that you'll still keep your promise.

94
00:07:44,478 --> 00:07:46,478
That's why I'll get back to Saba Odi too.

95
00:07:47,478 --> 00:07:48,478
At any cost!

96
00:07:59,478 --> 00:08:00,478
It's about time.

97
00:08:00,478 --> 00:08:03,478
I knew you guys weren't gonna let me go that easily.

98
00:08:03,478 --> 00:08:16,478
That's my full demon technique!

99
00:08:16,478 --> 00:08:17,478
And that's the Dragon Twister!

100
00:08:17,478 --> 00:08:26,478
They've learned to copy my three-sword style!

101
00:08:26,478 --> 00:08:27,478
Hey, Shelps!

102
00:08:27,478 --> 00:08:28,478
Copying me?

103
00:08:28,478 --> 00:08:29,478
Pathetic!

104
00:08:29,478 --> 00:08:32,478
How can you be satisfied with yourselves?

105
00:08:32,478 --> 00:08:33,478
You aren't real swordsmen?!

106
00:08:33,478 --> 00:08:34,478
Damn it!

107
00:08:34,478 --> 00:08:35,478
You can't mess with me like that!

108
00:08:35,478 --> 00:08:36,478
After all I've done for him, he doesn't appreciate anything!

109
00:08:36,478 --> 00:08:37,478
I hope he drops dead.

110
00:08:37,478 --> 00:08:38,478
Yeah, that'd serve him right and I wouldn't care one bit!

111
00:08:38,478 --> 00:08:48,478
If you're that worried about Roronoa, go AFRARA mailing

112
00:08:53,478 --> 00:08:55,478
If you're that worried about RORO NOAA!

113
00:08:55,478 --> 00:08:56,478
Go L saved you guys, find me.

114
00:08:56,478 --> 00:08:58,478
That's a natural man!

115
00:08:58,478 --> 00:09:07,478
Is he okay if you'd come back?

116
00:09:07,478 --> 00:09:09,078
Oh, uh, go look for him.

117
00:09:09,518 --> 00:09:10,978
You think I'm worried about him?

118
00:09:11,138 --> 00:09:12,778
What gave you that impression, huh?

119
00:09:13,718 --> 00:09:17,058
In any case, I don't think he'll die so easily.

120
00:09:17,718 --> 00:09:19,358
Yeah? You're wrong.

121
00:09:19,478 --> 00:09:22,178
By the time Kuma got to him, he was already banged up,

122
00:09:22,198 --> 00:09:24,938
and since he showed up at the castle, he's only gotten worse.

123
00:09:25,598 --> 00:09:28,678
And those baboons don't exactly strike me as the merciful type.

124
00:09:30,138 --> 00:09:32,678
Damn, damn, damn! This isn't fair!

125
00:09:33,098 --> 00:09:37,118
If Zoro gets himself killed out there, I'll be stuck with Hawkeye.

126
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,838
And he's downright rude to my stuffed animals.

127
00:09:40,178 --> 00:09:43,838
And as a host, he hasn't offered me hot cocoa, not even one time!

128
00:09:44,178 --> 00:09:45,698
You may be kind of an oaf, Zoro,

129
00:09:45,798 --> 00:09:48,898
but you're still a lot more fun to have around than that old dirtbag!

130
00:09:50,158 --> 00:09:52,238
So don't get killed out there, okay?

131
00:10:00,478 --> 00:10:01,838
3,000 worlds!

132
00:10:07,118 --> 00:10:13,678
But why?

133
00:10:14,178 --> 00:10:15,378
Scars on the back.

134
00:10:15,958 --> 00:10:17,118
Or swordsman's shame.

135
00:10:18,298 --> 00:10:18,978
Fine.

136
00:10:18,978 --> 00:10:35,638
Yuh-hoo! Zoro!

137
00:10:35,938 --> 00:10:37,038
Are you still alive?

138
00:10:37,038 --> 00:10:40,678
I haven't spotted a single sign of him all day.

139
00:10:41,098 --> 00:10:42,418
But he couldn't have set sail!

140
00:10:42,958 --> 00:10:43,258
No.

141
00:10:43,658 --> 00:10:45,518
No, don't tell me he got lost again.

142
00:10:49,938 --> 00:10:50,518
Honey?

143
00:10:52,098 --> 00:10:52,818
Giddy!

144
00:10:52,818 --> 00:11:03,558
You can't fix that with your spits!

145
00:11:03,778 --> 00:11:05,898
Who even taught you that garbage, your grandma?

146
00:11:10,858 --> 00:11:11,298
Bastards!

147
00:11:11,718 --> 00:11:14,058
They may be stupid, but damn, they're strong.

148
00:11:14,858 --> 00:11:17,218
At this rate, I'm never going to make it to the sea.

149
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:27,718
Hawkeye.

150
00:11:29,258 --> 00:11:31,698
It's been quite a while since you left the castle,

151
00:11:31,958 --> 00:11:33,558
yet you've only made it this far.

152
00:11:33,978 --> 00:11:34,238
Pity.

153
00:11:34,898 --> 00:11:36,198
And the boat I offered you,

154
00:11:36,398 --> 00:11:38,638
it seems it's not seaworthy now.

155
00:11:39,498 --> 00:11:40,178
Shut up!

156
00:11:40,518 --> 00:11:41,198
It's fine!

157
00:11:41,358 --> 00:11:43,698
We can just hold on to a few planks and swim there.

158
00:11:43,858 --> 00:11:45,878
I'm not one to give up that easily, alright?

159
00:11:45,878 --> 00:11:47,958
Your sentiment is admirable,

160
00:11:48,678 --> 00:11:50,498
but you can't defeat them.

161
00:11:51,478 --> 00:11:52,678
They're called humandrils,

162
00:11:53,158 --> 00:11:55,958
baboons that develop by imitating human behavior.

163
00:11:56,818 --> 00:11:57,378
Humandrils?

164
00:11:58,058 --> 00:12:00,718
Had they grown up among peace-loving humans,

165
00:12:00,938 --> 00:12:02,358
they would have turned out differently.

166
00:12:02,898 --> 00:12:04,538
But not on this island.

167
00:12:05,838 --> 00:12:07,738
Up until seven years ago,

168
00:12:07,918 --> 00:12:09,618
this was the site of a great war.

169
00:12:09,618 --> 00:12:12,938
When I first came here to live,

170
00:12:13,498 --> 00:12:16,578
the entire island still smelled of blood and smoke.

171
00:12:17,198 --> 00:12:19,578
Everywhere, dead bodies littered the ground.

172
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:22,078
As the battles raged on,

173
00:12:22,178 --> 00:12:25,078
these baboons watched the violence between the humans unfold.

174
00:12:25,698 --> 00:12:28,278
In time, they learned how to use human weapons and armor,

175
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:30,118
becoming warriors of the forest.

176
00:12:31,398 --> 00:12:34,898
Humans can defeat ordinary animals by using weapons and intellect.

177
00:12:34,898 --> 00:12:38,298
But what happens when animals don weapons as well?

178
00:12:38,978 --> 00:12:39,818
As you can see,

179
00:12:39,938 --> 00:12:42,858
they make formidable opponents for an arrogant young man.

180
00:12:42,958 --> 00:12:44,178
You talking about me?

181
00:12:44,338 --> 00:12:45,418
Well, who else?

182
00:12:46,158 --> 00:12:47,398
Now, let's leave.

183
00:12:47,838 --> 00:12:48,358
It's late.

184
00:12:48,938 --> 00:12:51,418
The humandrils won't set foot near the castle.

185
00:12:52,498 --> 00:12:53,058
Yeah?

186
00:12:53,278 --> 00:12:55,278
You got no right telling me what to do.

187
00:12:55,998 --> 00:12:58,178
I've got to make it to the sea.

188
00:12:58,898 --> 00:12:59,838
Of course.

189
00:13:01,218 --> 00:13:02,338
Do as you like.

190
00:13:02,338 --> 00:13:07,518
I don't care if they're forest warriors or monkeys.

191
00:13:08,198 --> 00:13:10,898
I've already wasted enough time stranded in this dump.

192
00:13:12,778 --> 00:13:15,138
I'm cutting down every single one of them.

193
00:13:15,338 --> 00:13:16,058
Come on.

194
00:13:16,458 --> 00:13:18,398
That doof's got to be around here somewhere.

195
00:13:20,478 --> 00:13:20,998
There.

196
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:23,018
But the baboon's got to it first.

197
00:13:26,298 --> 00:13:27,498
Zoro, no!

198
00:13:27,498 --> 00:13:27,618
No!

199
00:13:32,338 --> 00:13:51,978
Meanwhile, in the land of Hungaria, on Lazy Bones Island...

200
00:13:51,978 --> 00:13:55,518
What is he doing?

201
00:13:55,698 --> 00:13:56,978
He's been in that shack forever.

202
00:13:57,238 --> 00:14:00,118
If Lord Satan's going to help us curse the Longarm Tribe,

203
00:14:00,318 --> 00:14:02,098
then how come it's so quiet?

204
00:14:02,578 --> 00:14:04,538
Lord Satan knows what he's doing.

205
00:14:04,958 --> 00:14:09,198
There's no doubt in my mind that our Savior is bringing forth a powerful incantation

206
00:14:09,198 --> 00:14:11,858
to deal the tyrannical Longarm Tribe a fatal blow.

207
00:14:12,218 --> 00:14:13,718
Ho-ho-ho-ho-ho-ho!

208
00:14:13,718 --> 00:14:15,338
Greetings, everyone.

209
00:14:15,538 --> 00:14:16,438
Thank you for waiting.

210
00:14:17,118 --> 00:14:18,838
Is the ritual finally over?

211
00:14:19,598 --> 00:14:20,898
Atta boy, Satan!

212
00:14:21,278 --> 00:14:22,918
My work is now complete.

213
00:14:23,238 --> 00:14:24,478
I hope it will do the trick.

214
00:14:25,438 --> 00:14:26,678
What is he holding?

215
00:14:27,138 --> 00:14:28,018
And here you go.

216
00:14:28,918 --> 00:14:30,518
Oh, thank you, Lord.

217
00:14:30,858 --> 00:14:31,698
What is it?

218
00:14:31,758 --> 00:14:32,818
Just a little ditty.

219
00:14:33,178 --> 00:14:33,698
Wait, no!

220
00:14:33,978 --> 00:14:34,738
Don't tell me!

221
00:14:34,898 --> 00:14:35,418
Huh?

222
00:14:36,698 --> 00:14:38,898
Our prayers have finally been answered.

223
00:14:39,258 --> 00:14:42,738
Satan has pinned a set of talismans to help us kill the Longarm Tribe.

224
00:14:42,978 --> 00:14:46,098
Lord Satan has doomed the Longarms to an agonizing death.

225
00:14:46,458 --> 00:14:46,898
Huh?

226
00:14:47,318 --> 00:14:49,038
We're now as good as invincible.

227
00:14:49,378 --> 00:14:53,178
Try as they might, even those Longarm bullies can't lay their hands on us anymore.

228
00:14:54,118 --> 00:14:56,898
I bet the mere sight of these symbols will strike them dead.

229
00:14:57,178 --> 00:14:58,178
Not exactly.

230
00:14:58,538 --> 00:14:59,158
How awesome!

231
00:14:59,418 --> 00:15:00,578
That's Lord Satan for you.

232
00:15:00,878 --> 00:15:01,758
Come on, men!

233
00:15:01,938 --> 00:15:05,378
Everybody grab a page and find a place to nail it up around town!

234
00:15:05,558 --> 00:15:06,318
Be quick!

235
00:15:06,438 --> 00:15:07,918
No, it's not like that.

236
00:15:07,978 --> 00:15:09,318
You really shouldn't separate them!

237
00:15:09,738 --> 00:15:10,018
Oh.

238
00:15:10,018 --> 00:15:15,918
Oh, goodness!

239
00:15:16,918 --> 00:15:17,258
Hello!

240
00:15:19,758 --> 00:15:21,178
They're all posted now.

241
00:15:21,958 --> 00:15:22,398
Yes.

242
00:15:22,618 --> 00:15:23,638
Excellent work, friends.

243
00:15:24,378 --> 00:15:26,178
I finally feel safe now.

244
00:15:26,578 --> 00:15:28,038
We all owe you our lives.

245
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:28,938
Thank you, Lord.

246
00:15:29,358 --> 00:15:30,118
Uh...

247
00:15:30,118 --> 00:15:30,518
Sir!

248
00:15:30,678 --> 00:15:31,498
We have a problem!

249
00:15:31,498 --> 00:15:34,598
The Longarm Tribe is on their way here!

250
00:15:34,598 --> 00:15:37,938
Those simpletons are like moths to a flame.

251
00:15:38,398 --> 00:15:42,838
Now we sit back and watch, for as of today, our enemies are history!

252
00:15:43,978 --> 00:15:45,038
Hold on!

253
00:15:45,458 --> 00:15:47,978
Um, that thing with all the pages?

254
00:15:48,338 --> 00:15:51,598
It's actually a musical score, not a talisman at all.

255
00:15:51,798 --> 00:15:52,218
Huh?

256
00:15:53,318 --> 00:15:53,958
What?

257
00:15:53,958 --> 00:16:02,258
Well, we're dead.

258
00:16:03,638 --> 00:16:04,978
They'll take our food.

259
00:16:05,418 --> 00:16:07,918
What few things of value we have, they'll claim as their own.

260
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:09,198
People will be kidnapped.

261
00:16:09,658 --> 00:16:10,638
Life will be miserable.

262
00:16:11,298 --> 00:16:12,778
We have no choice.

263
00:16:13,938 --> 00:16:15,778
You always have a choice.

264
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:17,518
Lord Satan.

265
00:16:20,258 --> 00:16:23,058
Please, lend me your ears, if you would.

266
00:16:23,058 --> 00:16:32,358
This song?

267
00:16:32,618 --> 00:16:33,478
What's it doing?

268
00:16:33,918 --> 00:16:36,858
It's as if my body is filling with a brand new energy!

269
00:16:39,738 --> 00:16:41,998
What the hell is this?

270
00:16:42,118 --> 00:16:43,058
Some kind of spell?

271
00:16:43,438 --> 00:16:47,418
Not only do people with one joint in their arm look funny, but they think funny, too.

272
00:16:47,418 --> 00:16:49,038
What are they up to this time?

273
00:16:49,038 --> 00:16:50,038
Huh?

274
00:16:54,038 --> 00:16:55,758
Well now, what's this?

275
00:16:55,758 --> 00:17:03,078
From this day forth, we no longer allow the Long-Arm Tribe to terrorize our people.

276
00:17:03,618 --> 00:17:04,098
Huh?

277
00:17:04,318 --> 00:17:05,058
That's right!

278
00:17:05,218 --> 00:17:06,818
We're finally fighting back!

279
00:17:06,958 --> 00:17:07,338
Yeah!

280
00:17:07,518 --> 00:17:09,258
You're not taking anything else from us!

281
00:17:09,338 --> 00:17:12,198
We're gonna protect that which is ours with our own hands!

282
00:17:12,398 --> 00:17:13,518
Make your move!

283
00:17:13,798 --> 00:17:14,958
We're not afraid of you!

284
00:17:14,958 --> 00:17:17,418
Now you've got it!

285
00:17:17,718 --> 00:17:20,458
Hey, boss, they're acting kind of different than usual.

286
00:17:21,058 --> 00:17:21,698
All right.

287
00:17:22,158 --> 00:17:24,838
Guess we need to remind these short-arms we own them!

288
00:17:25,318 --> 00:17:25,718
Attack!

289
00:17:26,718 --> 00:17:27,898
Let's go!

290
00:17:32,898 --> 00:17:34,798
You're truly a blessing from hell.

291
00:17:35,098 --> 00:17:36,458
Thank you, Lord Satan.

292
00:17:36,458 --> 00:17:39,258
It's unreal.

293
00:17:39,638 --> 00:17:43,898
I never imagined that one day we'd be able to fight back like that, much less beat them

294
00:17:43,898 --> 00:17:45,098
and put them in a cage.

295
00:17:45,278 --> 00:17:45,798
The music!

296
00:17:46,118 --> 00:17:47,518
Something about it changed us!

297
00:17:47,898 --> 00:17:49,638
I've never felt so uplifted before!

298
00:17:50,018 --> 00:17:50,698
He's right!

299
00:17:50,898 --> 00:17:52,798
Courage and strength welled up in our hearts!

300
00:17:53,318 --> 00:17:56,438
We stood up and defended ourselves for the first time in our lives!

301
00:17:56,698 --> 00:17:56,838
Hmm.

302
00:17:57,638 --> 00:17:59,798
Of course we had no idea how to use our weapons.

303
00:18:00,498 --> 00:18:03,298
Ultimately, you did most of the actual fighting by yourself.

304
00:18:03,298 --> 00:18:04,258
But that's okay.

305
00:18:04,538 --> 00:18:07,258
What matters is the people who were abducted came back safely.

306
00:18:08,558 --> 00:18:11,498
No, you're too modest.

307
00:18:11,818 --> 00:18:13,338
I only helped a teeny bit.

308
00:18:14,178 --> 00:18:17,498
Neither gods nor devils will help those who won't fight on their own.

309
00:18:18,058 --> 00:18:21,438
In times like these, it is important to stand resolute against evil,

310
00:18:21,618 --> 00:18:23,138
even if the odds seem insurmountable.

311
00:18:23,718 --> 00:18:24,778
You have the courage.

312
00:18:24,918 --> 00:18:25,898
You prove that today.

313
00:18:26,258 --> 00:18:27,438
Such a wise god!

314
00:18:27,978 --> 00:18:29,258
You've inspired us!

315
00:18:29,458 --> 00:18:31,138
We'll do our best to make you proud!

316
00:18:31,378 --> 00:18:33,258
Thank you very much for your teaching!

317
00:18:33,498 --> 00:18:34,618
Hail, Lord, Satan!

318
00:18:35,378 --> 00:18:37,258
I hope that repaid their kindness.

319
00:18:38,758 --> 00:18:41,258
Still, I can't believe the news.

320
00:18:41,818 --> 00:18:43,318
Please stay strong, Luffy.

321
00:18:43,958 --> 00:18:44,978
I hope you're alright.

322
00:18:45,618 --> 00:18:47,638
I'll be there soon to share in your grief.

323
00:18:48,798 --> 00:18:50,478
If I had a heart, it would be heavy.

324
00:18:51,478 --> 00:18:53,138
Until I can return to your side,

325
00:18:53,198 --> 00:18:56,678
all I can do is play a song and hope that it reaches you somehow.

326
00:18:57,338 --> 00:18:57,938
Damn it!

327
00:18:58,078 --> 00:19:00,798
I can't believe they got the devil as their bodyguard.

328
00:19:00,798 --> 00:19:01,898
What an embarrassment!

329
00:19:02,338 --> 00:19:06,178
They should be the ones in cages with those freakish single-jointed arms of theirs on display.

330
00:19:06,598 --> 00:19:09,258
Actually, we could make a lot of money doing that, couldn't we?

331
00:19:10,038 --> 00:19:11,058
Good idea.

332
00:19:11,218 --> 00:19:11,418
Huh?

333
00:19:11,698 --> 00:19:14,798
We'll put their freakish double-jointed arms on display.

334
00:19:15,258 --> 00:19:18,638
They owe us, and we can certainly make a lot of money doing that.

335
00:19:18,838 --> 00:19:19,678
Wait just a minute!

336
00:19:19,898 --> 00:19:20,738
That's wrong!

337
00:19:20,798 --> 00:19:20,918
Huh?

338
00:19:20,918 --> 00:19:22,318
And it's immoral!

339
00:19:22,578 --> 00:19:25,658
I'm certain that you didn't appreciate it when they were cruel to you.

340
00:19:25,778 --> 00:19:26,138
Huh?

341
00:19:27,198 --> 00:19:28,778
Everyone, listen to me.

342
00:19:30,258 --> 00:19:31,418
Let them go?

343
00:19:31,678 --> 00:19:32,978
How could we, Lord Satan?

344
00:19:33,358 --> 00:19:35,298
They'll just come back and attack us again.

345
00:19:35,358 --> 00:19:36,318
No, they will not.

346
00:19:36,318 --> 00:19:39,958
I'll make sure of that by binding them to a devil's contract.

347
00:19:41,618 --> 00:19:43,318
Heed my words well.

348
00:19:44,098 --> 00:19:49,258
If you break your oath with me and commit a wrongful act against the people in this country

349
00:19:49,258 --> 00:19:52,118
again, I will hunt each of you down.

350
00:19:52,578 --> 00:19:54,738
And then I will eat your heart!

351
00:19:57,138 --> 00:19:58,058
Thank you, sir.

352
00:19:58,218 --> 00:19:59,978
We promise you will behave.

353
00:20:00,218 --> 00:20:01,978
We're going straight back to our homes.

354
00:20:02,298 --> 00:20:03,598
We'll never come back again.

355
00:20:03,598 --> 00:20:05,018
No, please don't hurt us.

356
00:20:05,558 --> 00:20:11,298
You three are free to go, but you must always remember, do not treat others poorly.

357
00:20:11,938 --> 00:20:16,158
If somebody went into your country causing havoc and destruction, then I'm sure you'd be

358
00:20:16,158 --> 00:20:16,558
unhappy.

359
00:20:17,358 --> 00:20:20,658
It doesn't matter if you have one or two joints in your arms.

360
00:20:21,718 --> 00:20:23,878
Deep down, we're all the same.

361
00:20:23,878 --> 00:20:25,758
So treat each other with respect.

362
00:20:26,138 --> 00:20:27,378
Yes, thank you!

363
00:20:30,858 --> 00:20:32,418
Now grab him!

364
00:20:32,418 --> 00:20:36,838
What's the big idea here?

365
00:20:37,078 --> 00:20:38,378
Away we go!

366
00:20:39,378 --> 00:20:41,618
Sorry, but we don't believe in curses.

367
00:20:42,038 --> 00:20:45,538
Also, your speech was stupid and you fell for the oldest trick in the book.

368
00:20:46,138 --> 00:20:49,618
If we bring back an actual walking, talking skeleton...

369
00:20:49,618 --> 00:20:51,098
We can make a whole ton of money!

370
00:20:51,178 --> 00:20:51,798
Wait a minute!

371
00:20:52,198 --> 00:20:53,058
Let me go!

372
00:20:53,358 --> 00:20:54,898
I have somewhere I need to be!

373
00:20:55,298 --> 00:20:55,918
Oh no.

374
00:20:57,078 --> 00:20:58,298
We have an emergency!

375
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,138
Lord Satan has just been kidnapped!

376
00:21:01,598 --> 00:21:04,518
Everyone, prepare to summon another devil!

377
00:21:04,758 --> 00:21:05,638
And fast!

378
00:21:05,838 --> 00:21:06,258
Yes!

379
00:21:06,338 --> 00:21:09,298
We can still summon devils with the magical power of underwear!

380
00:21:09,298 --> 00:21:15,878
Luffy, when you feel sad, just sing a song.

381
00:21:16,418 --> 00:21:18,038
Music is meant to make you happy.

382
00:21:18,678 --> 00:21:20,278
So sing as you wait for me.

383
00:21:20,698 --> 00:21:21,598
I'll try to.

384
00:21:22,058 --> 00:21:23,998
No, I will be there.

385
00:21:24,638 --> 00:21:27,758
Until then, if you can hear me...

386
00:21:27,758 --> 00:21:28,918
Sandra, help!

387
00:21:28,918 --> 00:21:40,338
Well then, that's it.

388
00:21:41,678 --> 00:21:42,638
I'm sorry.

389
00:21:43,278 --> 00:21:45,898
What did you just say to him?

390
00:21:46,258 --> 00:21:47,178
You heard.

391
00:21:47,538 --> 00:21:48,938
You were right here the whole time.

392
00:21:49,078 --> 00:21:49,558
No!

393
00:21:50,238 --> 00:21:52,858
I'm finding it difficult to understand your intentions.

394
00:21:53,838 --> 00:21:56,698
Surely you know what's going on in Luffy's mind right now.

395
00:21:57,058 --> 00:21:58,258
Think of all he's been through!

396
00:21:59,118 --> 00:22:02,078
Depending on your answer, I may not be able to forgive you!

397
00:22:03,078 --> 00:22:04,058
I agree.

398
00:22:04,758 --> 00:22:06,658
How dare you suggest such a thing!

399
00:22:07,098 --> 00:22:08,658
And so soon after the war!

400
00:22:09,238 --> 00:22:10,578
It's simply cruel!

401
00:22:11,438 --> 00:22:13,398
I made a suggestion, that's all.

402
00:22:14,338 --> 00:22:15,818
Only Luffy can decide.

403
00:22:16,458 --> 00:22:17,578
So what's your decision?

404
00:22:24,458 --> 00:22:25,518
I don't know.

405
00:22:26,578 --> 00:22:27,578
All my friends...

406
00:22:28,258 --> 00:22:33,338
I never want them to go through something like that again.

407
00:22:33,338 --> 00:22:41,118
If I do like you tell me to, will it help me protect them?

408
00:22:42,198 --> 00:22:44,758
No promises, but it's certainly worth a shot.

409
00:22:45,478 --> 00:22:49,078
That said, you do realize you have a lot of work to do.

410
00:22:49,078 --> 00:22:53,498
Okay.

411
00:22:53,498 --> 00:22:56,458
I've made up my mind.

412
00:22:58,458 --> 00:23:01,178
If you think I should, I'll go back.

413
00:23:02,178 --> 00:23:03,778
To Marineford!

414
00:23:03,778 --> 00:23:14,158
After learning of Ace's death, Sanji plots to return to Saba-Ori.

415
00:23:14,558 --> 00:23:19,558
However, his plans are thwarted when Ivankov makes his long-awaited return to the Kamabaka kingdom.

416
00:23:19,978 --> 00:23:24,278
Burning with determination, Sanji begins a fierce battle with his pride on the line.

417
00:23:24,278 --> 00:23:29,818
On the next, One Piece, a disaster for Sanji, the Queen's return to the kingdom.

418
00:23:30,318 --> 00:23:32,158
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

